# Notable commercial AWS boundary

Only for work under `s3_notable_pipeline_commercial/` in
`llm_notable_analysis`, read that directory's current `AGENTS.md` and the
[full boundary snapshot](../skills/notable-incident-workflow/references/commercial-aws-boundary.md).
Commercial scope is partition `aws`, region `us-east-1`; fail closed outside it.
The sibling `s3_notable_pipeline/` is out-of-scope production GovCloud: no edits,
imports, symlinks, deployments, migrations, deletions, cleanup or copied runtime
data/secrets/identifiers/endpoints. No destructive AWS deletion commands.
Before a live mutation, verify account, partition, region, role/profile, stack
and intended resources, and obtain explicit deployment approval. Use the existing
Terraform customer-default root; preserve the internal Python package identity
and copied contracts unless explicitly scoped otherwise.
